=== task: multi medium
title: What things cost
prompt: Choose **every** cost that is correct for a graph with V vertices and E edges.
* Checking for an edge u–v with a matrix: O(1) :: Right. One box.
* Listing u's neighbours with an adjacency list: O(degree of u) :: Right. The list holds exactly the neighbours.
* Visiting every neighbour of every vertex with a matrix: O(V²) :: Right. Every box of every row.
* Memory for an adjacency list: O(V + E) :: Right. One list per vertex plus the edge entries.
- Listing u's neighbours with a matrix: O(degree of u) :: The whole row must be scanned: O(V).
- Memory for a matrix: O(V + E) :: It's always O(V²).
hint: A matrix row has a box for every vertex.
hint: An adjacency list stores only the edges that exist.
right: Matrices give O(1) edge checks but O(V) neighbour lists and O(V²) memory; adjacency lists give O(degree) neighbour lists and O(V + E) memory.
wrong: A matrix spends a box on every pair: O(V²) memory and O(V) to scan a row, but O(1) to check one pair. Adjacency lists hold only real edges.

